NOTE ON DATA. These licences cover the code only. Data consumed and
redistributed by this project carries its own terms (all verified
2026-10-06; the publishers' licence pages as fetched are kept in
provenance.tar.gz in this repository's source-data release):

  * Street geometry and attributes derive from OpenStreetMap via Overture
    Maps and are (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed ODbL 1.0
    (https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/); a few hundred of the
    Overture records come from TomTom, also under ODbL 1.0. Derived street
    geometry in this repository -- including outputs/*.geojson,
    outputs/flat_corridors.*, outputs/*.csv, data/processed/edges_*.parquet,
    the interactive HTML maps and site/data/graph-*.bin.gz -- is a Derived
    Database under the ODbL and carries its share-alike obligations: it is
    made available under the ODbL 1.0, and the code that produces it from
    the sources is in this repository. The place search's mapped features
    (Overture base theme) and the OpenStreetMap incline tags used in
    validation are likewise (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0.
  * Elevation is swissALTI3D (and, for validation only, DHM25), (c) Federal
    Office of Topography swisstopo, used under swisstopo's terms of use for
    free geodata and geoservices (OGD): use, redistribution, processing and
    commercial use are permitted, and a source reference is mandatory. This
    project's source reference is "Federal Office of Topography swisstopo"
    (or "(c) swisstopo"), given on the site, on the static maps and in the
    README. Derived elevations (edge profiles, gradients, the hillshade) are
    "derived from swissALTI3D, Federal Office of Topography swisstopo".
  * Street addresses in the route finder's search come from the Official
    directory of building addresses (Amtliches Verzeichnis der
    Gebaeudeadressen), (c) Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, under the
    same OGD terms; opendata.swiss lists it as "Open use".
  * The statistical quarters (Statistische Quartiere) are published by the
    City of Zurich (Statistik Stadt Zuerich and the GIS-Zentrum, Geomatik +
    Vermessung) on data.stadt-zuerich.ch under Creative Commons CC0 1.0;
    no attribution is required, and the City is credited anyway.
  * Points of interest in the place search come from Overture Maps places,
    licensed CDLA Permissive 2.0 (https://cdla.dev/permissive-2-0/) for the
    Meta, Microsoft, PinMeTo and DAC records and CC0 1.0 for AllThePlaces.
    Overture's Foursquare records, licensed Apache 2.0, are left out.
  * zrh_flat_routes/vendor/ and site/leaflet-*.{js,css} contain Leaflet
    1.9.4, (c) 2010-2023 Vladimir Agafonkin, (c) 2010-2011 CloudMade,
    licensed BSD-2-Clause; its notice is in the vendored files and in
    zrh_flat_routes/vendor/README.md.
